<title>USA: Peoples Energy Q4 helped by higher rates.</title>
<headline>Peoples Energy Q4 helped by higher rates.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peoples Energy Corp said higher prices helped narrow the loss for its September fourth quarter, which is seasonally a weak quarter.</p>
<p>A one-time gain associated with termination of gas-storage contracts contributed to the fiscal year's strong showing, said chairman Richard Terry in a statement.</p>
<p>For the quarter, the company posted a loss of $0.26 per share compared with a year-ago loss of $0.38. For the full fiscal year, the utility had earnings of $2.96 per share, up from $1.78 in fiscal 1995.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
